{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia/issues/54306","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia/issues/54306/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia/issues/54306/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia/issues/54306/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/issues/54306","id":2269093417,"node_id":"I_kwDOABkWpM6HP54p","number":54306,"title":"`eigen` and `svd` with `Symmetric{Float16, ...}`","user":{"login":"btmit","id":14826039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODI2MDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14826039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit","html_url":"https://github.com/btmit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmit/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2024-04-29T13:43:49Z","updated_at":"2024-04-29T21:35:22Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"`eigen` and `svd` of `Symmetric{Float16, ...}` returns values with element type `Float32`. This is not the case when the input is not wrapped in `Symmetric`. `cholesky` decompositions don't have this issue.

```julia
a = rand(Float16, 3, 3);
a = a*a'
```

> svd(a)
SVD{Float16, Float16, Matrix{Float16}, Vector{Float16}}

> eigen(a)
Eigen{Float16, Float16, Matrix{Float16}, Vector{Float16}}

> cholesky(a)
Cholesky{Float16, Matrix{Float16}}

> svd(Symmetric(a))
SVD{Float32, Float32, Matrix{Float32}, Vector{Float32}}

> eigen(Symmetric(a))
Eigen{Float32, Float32, Matrix{Float32}, Vector{Float32}}

> cholesky(Symmetric(a))
Cholesky{Float16, Matrix{Float16}}



