https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/blob/10db2785521894dc4470e9c333ff7de22cc6862d/stdlib/LinearAlgebra/src/symmetriceigen.jl#L11 the matrix is promoted to `Float32` for LAPACK but the result is not cast back to `Float16`.

**Working cases:** For plain vanilla `svd(a)`, the result is cast back correctly in `svd.jl` and `eigen(a)` uses a specialised `Float16` routine in `eigen.jl`. Furthermore, for `cholesky`, there's a special method for `AbstractMatrix{Float16}` here: https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/blob/10db2785521894dc4470e9c333ff7de22cc6862d/stdlib/LinearAlgebra/src/cholesky.jl#L405 so the `cholesky(Symmetric(a))` function is Ok.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaLang/julia/issues/comments/2083720287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}}

